# Review ownership.
#
# The catch-all covers everything; the entries below it exist to make the
# high-consequence paths explicit, so that a change to inventory arithmetic or
# to a migration is visibly a different kind of change from a copy edit.

*                               @jasonc123456

# The inventory rules and the authorization model. A defect here is an oversell
# or a cross-business data leak, and neither is caught by a passing build.
/packages/domain/               @jasonc123456
/packages/authz/                @jasonc123456

# Applied migrations are immutable. A change under this path is either a new
# forward migration or a mistake.
/packages/db/migrations/        @jasonc123456

# Supply chain and release. Changes here alter what runs in CI with what
# permissions, and what ends up in a published image.
/.github/workflows/             @jasonc123456
/pnpm-workspace.yaml            @jasonc123456
/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @jasonc123456

# The canonical specification and the decision record.
/docs/adr/                      @jasonc123456
